  m_text: "Boulder density\nMass: Mass is the amount of matter an object is made
    of. It is an intrinsic property that does not change, regardless of where the
    object is (on Earth, on the Moon, in space). It is measured in kilograms (kg)
    or grams (g).\nVolume: Volume is the space an object occupies. It's \"how much
    space\" it takes up. It is measured in cubic meters (m\xB3), liters (l) or cubic
    centimeters (cm\xB3).\nThe ratio of how much mass we have in a certain unit of
    volume defines what the density is. Objects of the same volume could have a different
    density depending on the amount of mass contained within them.\nThe formula with
    which we obtain density is:"
