--- !u!114 &408071078
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 408071076}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Inertia\nRotational inertia (or moment of inertia) is the \"resistance\"
    of an object to rotate. The harder it is to spin an object, the more inertia
    it has. The inertia for any object that can be spun is based on its mass and
    that object's radius. However, each inertia is differentiated by how the mass
    is distributed inside the object. The inertial constant (k) is a number that
    depends on the shape of the object. It just tells you \"how the mass is distributed\"
    within that object. In classical three-dimensional shapes, it tells us how far
    the mass is distributed from the center of the object.\nWhen an object goes down
    a ramp, gravity must divide between:\n1. Translation movement (sliding down)\n2.
    Rotating movement (turning)\nIf an object has more inertia, it must use more
    energy to spin and therefore less energy to descend quickly. The less inertia
    it has, the less energy it wastes, the faster it drops.\nIn the ramp, our inclined
    plane, the height is calculated with respect to the sine of the angle multiplied
    by the length of the extended ramp: h= L sin \u0398.\nWhile the speed of a body
    on an inclined plane changes with respect to the height at which the ramp is
    placed. The more height we have, the faster the object will go. Obviously, since
    a rigid body such as a cylinder or sphere is descending from the ramp, for the
    previous discussion the speed will also be influenced by the inertial constant:"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
