  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Libra\nVolume is the space that an object occupies. It's like saying \"how
    much space does it take up\" in space. The shape of the object changes the volume,
    even though they may have the same weight. Volume is often based on the diameter
    of the object itself and the depth that the object has. For example, a cylinder
    has a base with a certain diameter corresponding to \\operatorname{r}^2:\n\n\nWhile
    the depth is relative to the height of the cylinder. This same reasoning can
    be used for shapes such as that of the classic cube where the height, length
    and depth value is the same. Well, if we think about it, the side is the extended
    internal diameter of the cube: \n\n\n\nUsing a tool such as a balance we can
    obtain the density of an object. Knowing the volume and mass it will be easy
    to use the density formula to arrive at the solution.\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
